  "title": "Erdős Problem #712",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Determine, for any $k>r>2$, the value of $ \\frac{\\mathrm{ex}_r(n,K_k^r)}{\\binom{n}{r}}, $ where $\\mathrm{ex}_r(n,K_k^r)$ is the largest number of $r$-edges which can placed on $n$ vertices so that there exists no set of $k$ vertices which is covered by all $\\binom{k}{r}$ possible $r$-edges.",
